# SMTP credential template for Vaultwarden's own outbound mail (invite/2FA emails).
# Version: 1.0.0
#
# This is the one credential in the whole Phase 4 design that cannot itself
# live in the vault (the vault cannot unlock itself to hand out its own mail
# credential). Reuse an existing sending account rather than minting a new one -
# one exception that exists in exactly this one place, not duplicated per node.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Fill in the real values below.
#   2. Copy the filled-in lines into ../.env (the file docker-compose.yml
#      actually reads) — then RESTORE THIS FILE to placeholders again. Never
#      leave real credentials sitting in a file named *.template.
#   3. Run: docker compose up -d --force-recreate
#   4. Confirm no crash-loop: docker logs vaultwarden --tail 20
#      (Vaultwarden hard-fails at startup on an invalid SMTP_FROM — a real
#      address is required, not a placeholder, or it will not start at all.)
#
# Fields:
SMTP_HOST=CHANGEME                # e.g. smtp.yourprovider.com
SMTP_PORT=CHANGEME                # 587 = STARTTLS (recommended), 465 = implicit TLS, 25 = unencrypted (avoid)
SMTP_SECURITY=CHANGEME            # starttls | force_tls | off
SMTP_USERNAME=CHANGEME            # usually the full sending address
SMTP_PASSWORD=CHANGEME            # app-specific password if the provider supports it, not the account login password
SMTP_FROM=CHANGEME                # must be a real, valid-looking email address — Vaultwarden validates this at boot
SMTP_FROM_NAME=CHANGEME           # display name on outgoing mail, cosmetic only
